```javascript
// Set up an interval to call a function every 500ms
setInterval(function() {
    console.log("Hello World!");
}, 500);
```

In this example, the `console.log` statement will be executed every 500 milliseconds (which is equivalent to 5 seconds).

If you want to set the interval to run for a longer duration, you can pass a number as the second argument to the `setInterval` function.

For instance, if you wanted to run the same log message every 10 seconds instead of every 500ms, you would write:

```javascript
setInterval(function() {
    console.log("Hello World!");
}, 10000);
```

This sets the interval to run every 10 seconds.
